        "nobel_worthiness": "A profound, broadly applicable account of irreversibility and work fluctuations that made nonequilibrium statistical mechanics quantitatively predictive.",
        "attribution": "Evans and Gallavotti supplied central fluctuation relations, while Jarzynski provided the influential equality linking nonequilibrium work to equilibrium free energies.",
        "maturity": "The results are theoretically clean, extensively tested, and have shaped experiments from single molecules to quantum thermodynamics.",
