      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Two-dimensional conformal field theory revealed an exceptionally powerful universal structure, transforming critical phenomena and quantum field theory.",
        "attribution": "The credited trio established the defining framework and its decisive use of conformal symmetry.",
        "maturity": "Its consequences have endured for decades across statistical physics, condensed matter, and string theory.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its strongest impact is theoretical and distributed across several fields, which can complicate a single-prize framing."
