        "Antoine Georges",
        "Dieter Vollhardt",
        "Gabriel Kotliar"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory supplied a controlled conceptual and computational framework for electronic correlations in real materials.",
        "attribution": "Vollhardt's infinite-dimensional construction and the Georges-Kotliar formulation made the method broadly usable and physically decisive.",
        "maturity": "It is a mature standard of correlated-electron physics, repeatedly connected to experiments and material-specific calculations.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The development involved a wider community, particularly in extensions and applications."
