        "John Toner",
        "Sriram Ramaswamy",
        "Tamás Vicsek"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The discovery that collective active systems possess new hydrodynamic laws and long-range order is a fundamental advance in statistical physics.",
        "attribution": "Vicsek demonstrated the striking collective phenomenon, while Toner and Ramaswamy developed its essential continuum theoretical understanding.",
        "maturity": "The framework has generated a large experimental and theoretical field, with relevance from colloids to living matter.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Real biological systems are diverse, and the boundary between a universal mechanism and model-dependent phenomenology remains debated."
        ]
      }
    },
