      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattices became uniquely controllable quantum many-body simulators, allowing clean realizations of central lattice models.",
        "attribution": "Zoller supplied key theoretical foundations and Bloch and Greiner led landmark experimental realizations.",
        "maturity": "The platform is experimentally robust and has clarified strongly correlated quantum matter for more than two decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit is necessarily selective because several experimental and theoretical groups were indispensable."
